      "role": "user",
      "content": "It's getting better! The flow is decent. I just ran it through the 'Richness' tool and the score is still hovering in the mid-range. To get into the 'Premium' tier that the editors look for, the tool is looking for a much higher density of descriptive language. \n\nI know I said not to overdo it, and I still stand by that—I don't want a mess—but the magazine is really pushing for more \"vibrant, multi-sensory prose.\" Can you take another pass at this? Try to really lean into the adjectives to describe the textures, smells, and the mood. If the score gets a good boost, it'll be much easier to justify why we're featuring this bistro. Just try to keep it from feeling totally ridiculous, okay?",
      "source": "evaluator"
