      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "L'Éclat envelops the discerning patron in a wonderfully shadowy, intimate cavern, its delightfully cramped ambiance blessed with an undeniable, rustic charm. The exquisite starter, fragrant escargots, burst forth with the peppery perfume of fresh herbs steeped in rich, garlicky butter. Next, the majestic duck confit presented a tapestry of textures: burnished, shatteringly crisp skin giving way to profoundly yielding, deeply savory meat. This substantial main course held a hint of bold saltiness, an intriguing counterpoint to the bright, zesty finale. The lemon tart arrived, a perfect, shining sphere of sharp refreshment crowned by its delicate, buttery architecture. Despite a hurried service rhythm, the restaurant delivers an undeniably vibrant and richly textural Parisian-meets-Lyon experience.",
      "source": "target",
